# rlx-voxtral-tts

Mistral **Voxtral-4B-TTS** ([mistralai/Voxtral-4B-TTS-2603](https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Voxtral-4B-TTS-2603)) for RLX — a native Rust port of the vLLM-Omni `VoxtralTTSAudioGeneration` pipeline (Ministral LM + acoustic flow matching + codec decode), with no Python at inference.

## Quick start

```bash
just voxtral-tts -- \
  --model-dir .cache/voxtral/Voxtral-4B-TTS-2603 \
  --text "Hello from Voxtral." --voice neutral_female -o out.wav

# Or directly:
cargo run -p rlx-voxtral-tts --release -- --model-dir DIR --text "..." -o out.wav
```

Fetch the checkpoint with `just fetch-voxtral-tts`. Key CLI flags:

| Flag | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `--model-dir` / `--weights` | Voxtral-4B-TTS checkpoint dir |
| `--text` / `-o` | Prompt text / output WAV |
| `--voice` / `-v` | Preset voice name (`--list-voices`) |
| `--reference-wav` | Clone from mono reference audio (needs encoder in checkpoint) |
| `--encode-reference` / `--voice-embedding` | Save / reuse a pre-encoded `.f32` voice |
| `--decode-codes` | Decode a saved codes file straight to WAV |
| `--cfg-alpha` / `--seed` / `--max-frames` | Generation controls |
| `--eager-lm` / `--eager-acoustic` | Hand-ported CPU stacks (parity / debug) |
| `--device` | `cpu` (default) or a compiled GPU backend |

## Public API

```rust
use rlx_voxtral_tts::{VoxtralTtsRunner, GenerationConfig, PRESET_VOICES};
use rlx_runtime::Device;

let mut runner = VoxtralTtsRunner::builder()
    .model_dir("Voxtral-4B-TTS-2603")
    .device(Device::Metal)
    .build()?;

let gen = GenerationConfig::default();
// Preset voice → WAV (tokenize text yourself, or use the CLI end-to-end).
runner.synthesize_native(&prompt_tokens, "neutral_female", out_wav, &gen)?;

// Voice cloning from a reference clip:
runner.synthesize_cloned_with_text("Some new text.", reference_wav, out_wav, &gen)?;
```

Preset names are in [`PRESET_VOICES`]. Other entry points: `synthesize_native_with_voice`,
`synthesize_native_from_token_file`, `decode_codes_to_pcm`, and the voice-clone helpers
in `voice_clone` (`encode_reference_wav`, `clone_from_reference_audio`).

## How it fits

- Backbone LM (Ministral) via [rlx-llama32](../rlx-llama32); compiled through [rlx-flow](../rlx-flow) / [rlx-ir](../rlx-ir).
- Acoustic flow-matching head + codec decoder are native (`acoustic`, `codec` modules).
- Fine-tune / voice-clone training lives in [rlx-voxtral-tts-train](../rlx-voxtral-tts-train)
  (codec encoder + LoRA, injected back into `consolidated.safetensors`).

Feature bundles `metal`/`mlx`/`cuda`/`rocm`/`gpu`/`vulkan` (and `apple-silicon`,
`all-backends`, …) forward the device to `rlx-runtime`.
